{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/collections/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics","content_id":"f68d8468-c425-4b1c-a6ff-d56e9cb286ae","description":"Annual Official Statistics on the number and proportion of children living in low income families.","details":{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><div class=\"call-to-action\">\n  <p>For the latest release on 26 March 2026, there are revisions to the Before Housing Costs time-series at UK, regional and local area level. Data prior to 2022 is not available and there is no scheduled additional release later in the year.</p>\n\n  <p>Following the successful completion of discovery work and a public consultation, see <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics-2014-to-2024\">Children in low income families - After Housing Costs Consultation Note</a>, After Housing Costs local area child poverty statistics are also published in the latest release for financial year ending 2024 and 2025.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>For both Before and After Housing Costs, these annual statistics include counts of children by:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>geography, including by:\n    <ul>\n      <li>local authority</li>\n      <li>Westminster parliamentary constituency</li>\n      <li>Ward</li>\n      <li>Middle Super Output Area</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>year</li>\n  <li>age of child</li>\n  <li>gender of child</li>\n  <li>family type</li>\n  <li>work status of the family</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"call-to-action\">\n  <p>We invite comments on the value of the proposed statistics and on the methodology and scope for any future release. Email <a href=\"mailto:stats.consultation-2018@dwp.gov.uk\">stats.consultation-2018@dwp.gov.uk</a> with feedback and queries about the statistics.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2 id=\"explore-the-statistics-with-our-interactive-tool\">Explore the statistics with our interactive tool</h2>\n\n<p>Find further breakdowns of these statistics on <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://stat-xplore.dwp.gov.uk/\">Stat-Xplore</a>, an online tool for exploring some of <abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP’s</abbr> main statistics.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"future-releases-and-developments\">Future releases and developments</h2>\n\n<p>Find future release dates in the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/search/research-and-statistics?content_store_document_type=upcoming_statistics&amp;order=updated-newest\">statistics release calendar</a> and more about <abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> statistics on the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-work-pensions/about/statistics\">Statistics at <abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> page</a>.</p>\n\n<p>Future developments to <abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> official statistics and any changes to statistical methodology are outlined in the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/dwp-statistical-work-programme\">statistical work programme</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"tell-us-what-you-think\">Tell us what you think</h2>\n\n<p>Our statistical practice is regulated by the Office for Statistics Regulation (<abbr title=\"Office for Statistics Regulation\">OSR</abbr>). <abbr title=\"Office for Statistics Regulation\">OSR</abbr> sets the standards of trustworthiness, quality and value in the <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://code.statisticsauthority.gov.uk/the-code/\">Code of Practice for Statistics</a> that all producers of official statistics should adhere to. You are welcome to contact us directly with any comments about how we meet these standards.</p>\n\n<p>Email <a href=\"mailto:stats.consultation-2018@dwp.gov.uk\">stats.consultation-2018@dwp.gov.uk</a> with feedback and queries about the statistics.</p>\n\n<p>Alternatively, you can contact <abbr title=\"Office for Statistics Regulation\">OSR</abbr> by emailing <a href=\"mailto:regulation@statistics.gov.uk\">regulation@statistics.gov.uk</a> or via the <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://osr.statisticsauthority.gov.uk\"><abbr title=\"Office for Statistics Regulation\">OSR</abbr> website</a>.</p>\n\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"Added latest statistics release for 'Children in low income families: local area statistics 2022 to 2025' . A link to the existing 'Children in low income families - After Housing Costs Consultation Note' has also been added under the heading 'Consultation'.","public_timestamp":"2026-03-26T09:30:12Z"},{"note":"Details added about revisions to the 26 March 2026 release.","public_timestamp":"2026-01-29T09:30:08Z"},{"note":"The 'call to action' box has been updated.","public_timestamp":"2025-12-08T12:42:27Z"},{"note":"Added a link to the annual release of Children in low income families: local area statistics (data for 2014 to 2024), updated 'Children in low income families: local area statistics: background information and methodology' and also added a link to the consultation 'Children in low income families – After Housing Costs Consultation Note' .","public_timestamp":"2025-03-27T09:30:12Z"},{"note":"Update on methodology for these Official Statistics.","public_timestamp":"2024-12-13T15:53:48Z"},{"note":"The 'call to action' box has been updated to reflect the review of the methodology underpinning the Official Statistics.","public_timestamp":"2024-09-02T10:11:28Z"},{"note":"Added a link to the annual release of Children in low income families: local area statistics (data for 2014 to 2023).","public_timestamp":"2024-03-21T09:30:10Z"},{"note":"Added a link to the annual release of Children in low income families: local area statistics (data for 2014 to 2022).","public_timestamp":"2023-03-23T09:30:05Z"},{"note":"Added a link to the annual release of Children in low income families: local area statistics (data for 2014 to 2021).","public_timestamp":"2022-03-31T08:30:05Z"},{"note":"Added a link to the annual release of Children in low income families: local area statistics (data for 2014 to 2020). ","public_timestamp":"2021-03-25T09:30:05Z"},{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2020-03-26T00:00:00Z"}],"collection_groups":[{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\">\n</div>","documents":["f0a72d9c-088c-43b1-9df0-3bc30fe52502"],"title":"Latest release"},{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\">\n</div>","documents":["eee6dc5e-2b59-4b4a-bad8-a634273fb6c1","fd55662a-6215-43ab-a78d-b1defc5c0b0e","51601ea3-a43b-4feb-9fb2-2013d3c73616","05756179-58fa-498a-848d-cfe78db72bcf","8027eeef-4da8-45b9-ad7f-c0eda55da00f","f5aabb7c-6a01-42f8-ba8a-d5bca6784c77"],"title":"Previous release"},{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>We’ve published our <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/dwp-statistics-policies-and-procedures\">policies and procedures</a> for <abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> statistics in the interests of transparency and to comply with the UK Statistics Authority code of practice.</p>\n\n</div>","documents":["ab586e82-0c61-4187-8b98-cc4d0239b770"],"title":"Background information and methodology"},{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>A consultation on proposals for a new statistical series on After Housing Costs counts and proportions of children in low-income families was conducted in 2025. The consultation note was published with the local area statistics for 2014 to 2024.</p>\n\n</div>","documents":["eee6dc5e-2b59-4b4a-bad8-a634273fb6c1"],"title":"Consultation"},{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>Estimates of numbers in low income in a single year from <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/households-below-average-income-hbai--2\">Households Below Average Income</a> are available.</p>\n\n<p>Other related <abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> statistics include:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>\n    <p><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/family-resources-survey--2\"><abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> Family Resources Survey</a></p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/income-dynamics-statistics\"><abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> Income Dynamics</a></p>\n  </li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Indices of multiple deprivation by country are available:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>\n    <p><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/english-indices-of-deprivation\">English Indices of Deprivation</a></p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p><a rel=\"external\" href=\"http://gov.wales/wimd\">Welsh Index of Multiple Deprivation</a></p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p><a rel=\"external\" href=\"http://www.gov.scot/simd\">Scottish Index of Multiple Deprivation</a></p>\n  </li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Details of other National and Official Statistics produced by the Department for Work and Pensions can be found on the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-work-pensions/about/statistics\"><abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> statistics homepage</a> with a schedule of statistical releases over the next 12 months and a list of the most recent releases.</p>\n\n<p>In accordance with the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/announcements\">Code of Practice for Statistics</a>, all <abbr title=\"Department for Work and Pensions\">DWP</abbr> National Statistics are announced in the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/search/research-and-statistics?content_store_document_type=upcoming_statistics&amp;organisations%5B%5D=department-for-work-pensions&amp;order=updated-newest\">government statistics calendar</a>.</p>\n\n</div>","documents":["5f5598d6-7631-11e4-a3cb-005056011aef"],"title":"Related publications"}],"emphasised_organisations":["b548a09f-8b35-4104-89f4-f1a40bf3136d"],"first_public_at":"2020-03-26T00:00:00.000+00:00","headers":[{"id":"explore-the-statistics-with-our-interactive-tool","level":2,"text":"Explore the statistics with our interactive tool"},{"id":"future-releases-and-developments","level":2,"text":"Future releases and developments"},{"id":"tell-us-what-you-think","level":2,"text":"Tell us what you think"}],"political":false},"document_type":"document_collection","first_published_at":"2020-03-26T00:00:00+00:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/collections/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/collections/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics","base_path":"/government/collections/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics","content_id":"f68d8468-c425-4b1c-a6ff-d56e9cb286ae","document_type":"document_collection","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-03-26T09:30:12Z","schema_name":"document_collection","title":"Children in low income families: local area statistics","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics","withdrawn":false}],"documents":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/statistics/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics-2022-to-2025","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/statistics/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics-2022-to-2025","base_path":"/government/statistics/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics-2022-to-2025","content_id":"f0a72d9c-088c-43b1-9df0-3bc30fe52502","document_type":"official_statistics","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-03-26T09:30:12Z","schema_name":"publication","title":"Children in low income families: local area statistics 2022 to 2025","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics-2022-to-2025","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/statistics/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics-2014-to-2024","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/statistics/children-in-low-income-families-local-area-statistics-2014-to-2024","base_path":"/government/statistics/children-in